1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:01,440
What's going on, everybody?

2
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:06,760
For First We Feast, my name is Sean Evans, and you're watching Hot Ones, the show with hot questions and even hotter wings.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,260
I don't know why I said that.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,120
I just messed up, actually.

5
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:14,380
I was brewing some coffee, and I totally forgot about it.

6
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,380
So now it's cold, so I had to reheat it in the microwave.

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,260
Definitely not one of my brightest moments.

8
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:26,900
I'm in a bit of a goofy mood, so hopefully that will help me overcome this game.

9
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:30,220
Because this game is so frickin' scary, man.

10
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,000
Oh, God.

11
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:36,540
It's gonna be fine.

12
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:43,380
The thing that's so scary about this game is that you don't know when you're gonna get attacked.

13
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:59,360
Because there are holes everywhere, and you can hear the monster moving about, and it's just so unsettling to know that every time you pass one of those holes, arms could be coming out and grabbing your legs, you know?

14
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:02,040
Like, holy fuck, that's a scary-ass thought.

15
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:06,660
Also, uh, press button.

16
00:01:06,880 --> 00:01:07,180
There we go.

17
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:12,500
Okay.

18
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:14,340
What's the status here, eh?

19
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,000
Let's have a look-see.

20
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:18,380
Um...

21
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:20,100
I made it back, didn't I?

22
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,260
Yes!

23
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:22,600
We got the code.

24
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:29,440
Fortunately for us, the monster, or Lambert, was bugging a little bit last time.

25
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,140
Oh, what's the problem, step monster?

26
00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:32,780
Are you stuck?

27
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,100
You know?

28
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:35,720
Actually kinda helped us.

29
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,120
Let us escape.

30
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:38,720
Um...

31
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:40,140
What's the next step?

32
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:41,900
I guess we go to Arsenal, since we have the code.

33
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:43,740
But...

34
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,580
Let me see here.

35
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:46,960
Okay.

36
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:50,000
I'm kind of getting, uh, FOMO in terms of...

37
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,460
maybe having missed some codes...

38
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:54,760
in the first area there.

39
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:56,360
What's it called?

40
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:57,220
Soldier Quarters.

41
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,580
But I don't think I wanna go back.

42
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:01,860
No way.

43
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:05,460
So we go to Arsenal, and figure out what to do then.

44
00:02:06,820 --> 00:02:07,280
Right.

45
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,340
What were we supposed to do in Arsenal?

46
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:12,520
Let's see here.

47
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:12,980
Notes.

48
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,780
How to get the hell out of here.

49
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,800
The dynamite is locked in the Arsenal.

50
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:18,140
Okay.

51
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:23,120
The detonator handle is somewhere down in the Roman tunnels.

52
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:24,220
Shit.

53
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:29,000
Okay, so it's just one of, uh, potentially multiple things we need...

54
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:30,800
to get out of here.

55
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:32,880
Which is to be expected, I guess.

56
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:35,120
Now, what's the status with the generator?

57
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,160
We're still very full on that.

58
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:39,500
Perfect.

59
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,340
Let's just go immediately then.

60
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:43,500
I'm happy.

61
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:45,020
The question is, do we bring anything?

62
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:48,800
Uh, what about bullets?

63
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,000
How are we doing on that?

64
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:53,760
We have no bullets.

65
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:54,440
Crap.

66
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:57,680
Uh...

67
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:58,680
Well, shit.

68
00:02:58,680 --> 00:02:59,800
Maybe we bring a grenade.

69
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,420
In case we need to destroy something.

70
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,420
I would love to bring some meat.

71
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:06,960
In case we meet rats.

72
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:14,660
For use when in need of aid, signals with its brightly burning and loudly hissing flame can be thrown.

73
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:17,880
I wonder what the point of this is if the monster isn't scared of it.

74
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:23,900
Maybe to distract the monster, make it follow the flare while you run away.

75
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,720
Something like that, perhaps.

76
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:27,860
Uh, let's save the game.

77
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:30,100
And let's go.

78
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:32,400
Uh, let me just double check the map here.

79
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:34,220
So we go all the way down.

80
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,120
Okay, that's easy enough.

81
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:38,500
Uh, we don't need the gun, I guess, if we don't have any ammo.

82
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:40,360
Right?

83
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:45,280
And let's work on turning on these lamps.

84
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,560
As we go along.

85
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:51,450
Okay.

86
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,000
Beautiful.

87
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,480
Arsenal is...

88
00:03:58,480 --> 00:03:59,060
open.

89
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,500
Wait, I thought I needed a coat to open it.

90
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,960
It's already open?

91
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:11,040
Oh man, look at this place.

92
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:11,280
Oh.

93
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:15,060
Okay, I guess we just had a transition.

94
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:19,310
I don't want to sprint.

95
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:25,060
I'm looking for potential hiding spots already.

96
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:28,170
So tunnels.

97
00:04:28,790 --> 00:04:29,950
Oh shit.

98
00:04:30,650 --> 00:04:31,290
Roman tunnels?

99
00:04:32,930 --> 00:04:34,070
I see items in here.

100
00:04:36,570 --> 00:04:37,370
Is that meat?

101
00:04:39,290 --> 00:04:40,170
Oh hell yeah.

102
00:04:40,590 --> 00:04:42,290
What's the point of this piece of wood?

103
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,400
What can I do with that?

104
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,380
Maybe I can make a...

105
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:52,080
Still handgranate!

106
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,680
The German variety.

107
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:55,320
Eh.

108
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:57,000
Also, I see a hole over there.

109
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:57,540
That's not good.

110
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,080
That's how the monster's gonna get us.

111
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,500
Okay, so this one is locked.

112
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,040
Ooh, there's a trap.

113
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:07,740
Let's be careful.

114
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,100
We're also on a timer.

115
00:05:17,230 --> 00:05:18,870
Nothing ever is in these boxes.

116
00:05:18,870 --> 00:05:19,830
I almost stepped on it.

117
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:21,910
I don't want to go in there.

118
00:05:22,010 --> 00:05:22,290
No way.

119
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:26,070
Ooh, some kind of storage room here.

120
00:05:31,310 --> 00:05:31,870
Empty.

121
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:36,840
Oh, here we go.

122
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:38,560
Oh shit!

123
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:39,120
Ooh!

124
00:05:39,660 --> 00:05:40,080
Ooh!

125
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:42,340
Nothing.

126
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:42,760
Damn!

127
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:48,820
Grenade.

128
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,540
Nothing in there.

129
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:55,880
Explosive storage.

130
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:58,360
That's where we get the dynamite, I guess.

131
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:04,550
Oh no, inventory full.

132
00:06:05,290 --> 00:06:06,410
Ah, shit.

133
00:06:07,710 --> 00:06:10,050
Kinda want to go back and deposit some of the stuff I found.

134
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:11,850
Then again, empty bottle.

135
00:06:12,010 --> 00:06:12,910
Do we really need this?

136
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:19,280
Oh god, I hate that he just drops it on the floor like that.

137
00:06:24,470 --> 00:06:25,190
Oh, Jesus.

138
00:06:25,870 --> 00:06:27,510
Okay, so we need a combination here.

139
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:30,230
What am I seeing here?

140
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:32,390
Dynamite?

141
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:34,750
Obviously we can't get in here, right?

142
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:35,390
There's no way.

143
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:37,430
Yeah, we gotta somehow open that.

144
00:06:41,190 --> 00:06:43,230
Okay, so we could throw a grenade to open that door.

145
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:44,950
And I think I may do that.

146
00:06:46,650 --> 00:06:51,750
But let's plan our approach here because when we throw that grenade, the monster's gonna come for sure.

147
00:06:58,210 --> 00:06:58,570
Okay.

148
00:06:59,930 --> 00:07:01,090
Let me see what we have here.

149
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:03,570
There's nowhere to hide in here.

150
00:07:04,910 --> 00:07:06,150
At least not that I'm seeing.

151
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:09,950
So maybe we blow it and we just run back.

152
00:07:10,210 --> 00:07:11,490
That seems like a good idea actually.

153
00:07:12,190 --> 00:07:13,670
We blow it up, we run back immediately.

154
00:07:18,590 --> 00:07:19,250
Okay, here we go.

155
00:07:34,030 --> 00:07:35,990
Just run away, run away, run away, run away.

156
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:46,510
You can't come in here!

157
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:50,820
You can't come in here!

158
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:52,580
You bastard!

159
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,640
Oh, Jesus Christ!

160
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:59,920
Oh, my inventory is so full!

161
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,220
I guess we need the meat for something.

162
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:10,400
Am I hurt?

163
00:08:16,250 --> 00:08:17,010
Just use...

164
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:18,050
Okay, I'm not currently injured.

165
00:08:18,230 --> 00:08:18,510
Got it.

166
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:21,430
Can I not just drop this on the floor over here and then pick it up later?

167
00:08:22,590 --> 00:08:22,970
Like...

168
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:24,770
Oh, I didn't mean to do that.

169
00:08:24,910 --> 00:08:25,070
Whoops.

170
00:08:27,810 --> 00:08:28,210
Uh...

171
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:29,410
X is for dropping, right?

172
00:08:29,750 --> 00:08:30,010
Here.

173
00:08:31,490 --> 00:08:32,090
Yeah, look!

174
00:08:32,170 --> 00:08:33,110
I'm just gonna pick that up later.

175
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:36,170
We're totally cool.

176
00:08:36,270 --> 00:08:37,210
I'm gonna fill this up now.

177
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:46,980
Nice!

178
00:08:48,980 --> 00:08:50,320
Now we have two slots.

179
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,120
Uh...

180
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,860
This piece of wood...

181
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,620
I'm gonna throw this on the table as well.

182
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,100
This is so genius actually, what I'm doing here.

183
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:02,160
Gas mask...

184
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:07,350
Okay, let's try this.

185
00:09:07,930 --> 00:09:08,730
Uh, save the game now.

186
00:09:11,410 --> 00:09:11,850
There.

187
00:09:15,570 --> 00:09:16,170
Let's go.

188
00:09:18,270 --> 00:09:20,050
What do I have to defend myself with?

189
00:09:20,270 --> 00:09:20,890
Worst case.

190
00:09:21,110 --> 00:09:22,070
I guess I have a grenade.

191
00:09:25,370 --> 00:09:25,810
Uh...

192
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:27,190
Or the flare.

193
00:09:34,910 --> 00:09:36,590
I don't understand how this door is open.

194
00:09:37,110 --> 00:09:38,750
I mean, we got the arsenal code.

195
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:40,730
But...

196
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:42,990
Maybe the guy on the radio...

197
00:09:43,430 --> 00:09:44,210
Uh, opened the door.

198
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:47,070
I'm not entirely sure.

199
00:09:47,190 --> 00:09:49,510
Also, didn't we find something last time that I didn't read?

200
00:09:51,530 --> 00:09:52,910
Neuer's Journal Part 2.

201
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:56,850
Uh, 14th of May, 1916.

202
00:09:57,690 --> 00:10:00,830
I have spoken to none of what's written in those texts, I swear it.

203
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:05,030
But now LaRue comes out of the tunnels, claiming to have seen things described in them.

204
00:10:05,530 --> 00:10:08,630
My rational mind cannot accept that this might be a coincidence.

205
00:10:09,190 --> 00:10:10,850
Nor can it accept the alternative.

206
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:13,790
I have to tell the others what's written in these texts.

207
00:10:14,370 --> 00:10:14,770
Tell them.

208
00:10:15,170 --> 00:10:15,670
Warn them.

209
00:10:17,290 --> 00:10:18,050
18th of May.

210
00:10:18,710 --> 00:10:22,450
They've punished LaRue for speaking out about what he saw, and now Renard has sent for me.

211
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:24,550
I'm sure I'm about to be punished as well.

212
00:10:25,210 --> 00:10:32,510
We're stuck between the Germans in front of us, High Command behind us, and some other horrible force that seems to lurk in shadows all around us.

213
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:35,010
I fear we are now truly beyond God's reach.

214
00:10:36,450 --> 00:10:37,190
20th of May.

215
00:10:37,590 --> 00:10:40,290
I've been locked in Delpy's cells for the past two nights.

216
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:42,990
Renard's punishment for me speaking about the texts.

217
00:10:43,690 --> 00:10:45,010
Nightmare after nightmare there.

218
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:46,410
Dreams of darkness.

219
00:10:46,870 --> 00:10:47,730
Seductive darkness.

220
00:10:48,390 --> 00:10:49,270
Voices there.

221
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:50,370
Welcoming me.

222
00:10:50,870 --> 00:10:54,670
I returned to my bunk and was met with the men, all of whom now have tales to tell.

223
00:10:55,090 --> 00:10:57,070
Nicolet, Farber, Hulebeck?

224
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,190
On and on.

225
00:10:58,570 --> 00:10:59,810
They're all hearing things.

226
00:11:00,210 --> 00:11:00,930
Dreaming things.

227
00:11:01,570 --> 00:11:06,370
Nights are now spent in the grip of a fear that crawls up the spine and digs its claws behind the eyes.

228
00:11:06,730 --> 00:11:07,950
Piercing mind and soul.

229
00:11:08,650 --> 00:11:12,710
But after what happened to LaRue and me, none dare speak to the officers.

230
00:11:13,170 --> 00:11:14,450
Not even to Joubert.

231
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:16,910
And worse, raids are beginning again.

232
00:11:17,410 --> 00:11:18,710
I'm to go tomorrow night.

233
00:11:19,830 --> 00:11:20,430
23rd.

234
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:21,750
Back from the raid.

235
00:11:21,970 --> 00:11:22,590
Can't sleep.

236
00:11:22,990 --> 00:11:23,710
Shells falling.

237
00:11:24,010 --> 00:11:25,910
The soles of my boots are worn thin.

238
00:11:26,250 --> 00:11:27,890
My feet bloody and blistered.

239
00:11:28,250 --> 00:11:29,290
Lost too many out there.

240
00:11:29,530 --> 00:11:30,450
I feel trapped.

241
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:32,430
25th of May.

242
00:11:32,430 --> 00:11:35,870
Last night the entire barracks was awakened by the sounds from the tunnel.

243
00:11:36,310 --> 00:11:37,470
Nightly they grow louder.

244
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:39,790
When I slept I dreamt of other worlds.

245
00:11:40,070 --> 00:11:41,730
Of pain wrapped in ecstasy.

246
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:43,790
This morning we are all as ghosts.

247
00:11:44,430 --> 00:11:45,530
Things cannot continue this way.

248
00:11:45,990 --> 00:11:48,910
I will enter the tunnels and see if I can find some way to end this.

249
00:11:49,210 --> 00:11:50,390
For all our sakes.

250
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:52,390
Oh my god.

251
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:56,110
This guy is brave, man.

252
00:11:56,110 --> 00:11:57,690
He has some balls on him.

253
00:11:59,030 --> 00:12:00,330
He really did that, huh?

254
00:12:02,890 --> 00:12:04,110
I guess he didn't succeed.

255
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:06,670
Okay, this looks to be open now.

256
00:12:06,770 --> 00:12:06,910
Good.

257
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:12,420
Ammo!

258
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:17,900
Oh shit!

259
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,280
Okay!

260
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:20,780
Nice!

261
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:23,040
We need one of these things to remove traps.

262
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:24,940
What's this called?

263
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:26,160
A...

264
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,200
I don't know.

265
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:28,500
You know what I mean.

266
00:12:39,690 --> 00:12:40,370
Will we safe?

267
00:12:41,650 --> 00:12:42,370
Will we good?

268
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,520
Gonna grab that.

269
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:52,820
This sub-map has been added to the main map in the administration office.

270
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:53,940
Okay.

271
00:12:54,860 --> 00:12:56,280
So that leads to tunnels.

272
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:59,120
I'm in the clerk's office now.

273
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,400
Explosive storage is there.

274
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:04,540
We have storage area A and B.

275
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:05,580
I'm trying to...

276
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,580
Oh, please don't appear behind me.

277
